{% macro body(scope) %}
{% if scope.time %}
    t = jnp.asarray(t, dtype=float)  # an array: math out of its domain is nan, no error
{% endif %}
{% if scope.states %}
    # states
{% for x in scope.states %}
    {{ x.code }} = x[{{ x.index }}]{{ comment(x.comment) }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% if scope.constants %}
    # constants
{% for c in scope.constants %}
    {{ c.code }} = p[{{ c.index }}]{{ comment(c.comment) }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% if scope.assignments %}
    # assigned values and reaction rates
{% for a in scope.assignments %}
    {{ a.code }} = {{ a.expr }}{{ comment(a.comment) }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% endmacro %}
"""The ODE system of the model {{ model.id | docstring if model.id else "without id" }}{% if model.name and model.name != model.id %}: {{ model.name | docstring }}{% endif %}.

Written by sbmlode {{ model.sbmlode }}{% if model.source %} from {{ model.source | docstring }}{% endif %}, SBML L{{ model.level }}V{{ model.version }}.
{% set units = [] %}
{% for key, unit in model.units.items() if unit %}
{% set _ = units.append([key, unit]) %}
{% endfor %}
{% if units %}

Units of the model:

{{ table(units, 4, docstring) }}
{% endif %}
{% if states %}

States x:

{{ table([["", "id", "name", "unit"]] + rows(states, "index", "id", "name", "unit"), 4, docstring) }}
{% endif %}

`initial_values(p)` returns the initial states x0 and the constants p at t = 0,
`f_dxdt(t, x, p)` the rates of change of the states and `f_y(t, x, p)` the assigned
values y, the rules and the reaction rates. They are functions of JAX: `jax.jit`
compiles them, `jax.vmap` maps them over arrays and `jax.grad` differentiates them.
{% if options.simulator %}
`simulate(ts)` integrates the model with diffrax and returns the states, the assigned
values and the constants at the output times ts, `to_frame` a table of them, the file
run as a script prints the head of a simulation:

    ts = jnp.linspace(0.0, 10.0, 101)
    simulation = simulate(ts)
    # a simulation for each row of the constants ps
    xs = jax.vmap(lambda p: simulate(ts, p).x)(ps)
    # the gradient of a function of the simulation with respect to the constants
    gradient = jax.grad(lambda p: jnp.sum(simulate(ts, p).x ** 2))(P0)
{% endif %}
"""

